# Copy this to CICD_MLops/team1_dnn/.env and fill in your values
# NEVER commit the actual .env file (it's in .gitignore)
#
# These exact same variable names are used:
#   - Locally:  loaded automatically from this .env file via python-dotenv
#   - In CI:    injected from GitHub Actions Secrets (same names)
# So local and CI behave identically — no code changes needed between environments.
#
# ── Set these both locally (.env) AND as GitHub Actions Secrets ──────────────
#
# For LOCAL (dev server):           For CI/CD (prod server):
# ──────────────────────────        ────────────────────────────────────────────
MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI=https://dagshub.com/e.dejband/mlops-dev-tracking.mlflow
MLFLOW_TRACKING_USERNAME=e.dejband
MLFLOW_TRACKING_PASSWORD=<your_dagshub_token_from_dagshub_settings>
#
# GitHub Actions Secrets to create (use PROD DagsHub repo values):
# Go to: GitHub repo → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → New secret
#
# Secret name               │ Value
# ──────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI       │ https://dagshub.com/e.dejband/mlops-prod-tracking.mlflow
# MLFLOW_TRACKING_USERNAME  │ e.dejband
# MLFLOW_TRACKING_PASSWORD  │ <dagshub prod token>
# SECRET_TEST_DATA_B64      │ contents of Documents/secret_test_100_b64.txt
